<title>GERMANY: German Dec trade surplus 7.2 bln DM.</title>
<headline>German Dec trade surplus 7.2 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Dec 96   Nov 96	  Dec 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +7.2     +9.8	    +6.4</p>
<p> Current account	     -3.0     +0.4	    -4.6</p>
<p> Exports			 66.0     70.6	    63.4</p>
<p> Imports			 58.8     60.8	    57.0</p>
<p> Services			-3.9     -3.8	    -2.7</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -1.3     -1.3	    -0.2</p>
<p> Transfers		     -5.1     -4.4	    -7.7</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 +0.1     +0.1	    -0.4</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC    1996		1995</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +97.6	     +85.3</p>
<p> Current account		-26.6	     -29.9</p>
<p> Exports			  784.3	     749.5</p>
<p> Imports			  686.7	     664.2</p>
<p> Services			 -54.9	     -53.9</p>
<p> Wage and property income   -14.4		+0.4</p>
<p> Transfers			-53.1	     -58.6</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	  - 1.8	     - 3.1</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
